menu "W5500 Ethernet"

    config W5500_DIRECT_SPI
        bool "Drive GP-SPI2 and GDMA registers directly"
        default n
        help
            Use w5500_spi_direct.c, which programs GP-SPI2 and a GDMA channel itself, instead of
            ESP-IDF's spi_master (w5500_spi_idf.c). Estimated CPU per 1,316-byte datagram: 11 us
            sent and 21 us received, against 76 us and 90 us; no spi_master code in IRAM. The
            ESP-IDF backend stays the reference until the board shows that both agree.

    config W5500_SETTINGS_NVS
        bool "Keep the eth settings in NVS"
        default y
        help
            `eth <setting>` saves to NVS, and a start reads them back. Without it the settings
            live in RAM from boot and last until reset: no NVS code, flash writes or heap after
            boot (the receiver).

    config W5500_DEFAULTS
        string "Settings over the built-in defaults"
        default ""
        help
            `eth` settings separated by ';', applied over w5500_settings_default() at boot and by
            `eth defaults`, for example "ip 192.168.77.3/24;dest 192.168.77.1:1234".

endmenu
